# Repo-root `.env` — copy to `.env`. This is the only env file for local
# development; there is no `apps/web/.dev.vars`.
#
# Two consumers, one file:
#   1. process.env — drizzle-kit (packages/db/drizzle.config.ts) and the
#      wrangler CLI. Loaded by the `with-env` script (dotenv-cli).
#   2. The dev Worker's `env` binding — wrangler folds process.env into the
#      binding because `apps/web/wrangler.jsonc` declares `secrets.required`.
#      Only names listed there reach the Worker, so adding a new Worker secret
#      means adding it in both places (and to `apps/web/env.d.ts`).
#
# In production the Worker names are set with `wrangler secret put`.

# --- Cloudflare CLI + drizzle-kit (process.env only) ---
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""
CLOUDFLARE_DATABASE_ID=""
# D1-scoped, for drizzle-kit push/studio.
CLOUDFLARE_D1_TOKEN=""
# Broader, for `wrangler deploy`.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""

# --- Worker secrets (see secrets.required in apps/web/wrangler.jsonc) ---

# Signs session cookies and the local `/api/r2-upload` proxy URLs.
# Any long random string: `openssl rand -base64 32`.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# R2, for presigning game deploys via the S3 API. All three must be
# non-empty or the deploy router throws INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR (a missing
# value doesn't fail boot, it just disables deploys).
#
# Locally these can be dummy strings. On a `localhost[:port]` Host header the
# deploy router returns HMAC-signed `/api/r2-upload` / `/api/r2-download`
# proxy URLs, so bytes go through the Miniflare-simulated GAMES_BUCKET
# binding and the S3 keys are never used. Reaching the dev worker at
# `127.0.0.1` skips that proxy and presigns against real R2 — use
# `localhost`. See AGENTS.md → Rules that matter.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID="local"
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID="local"
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="local"

# Optional — enables `vg generate`. Leaving it empty logs a "missing required
# secrets" warning on dev boot and errors the media procedures at call time.
FAL_API_KEY=""

# The FAL_*_BASE_URL overrides in apps/web/env.d.ts are not secrets. To point
# at a fal mock, add them to `vars` in apps/web/wrangler.jsonc.

# --- Production ---
# `.env.production.local` (gitignored) holds the prod Cloudflare
# account/database/D1 token and is read only by `pnpm db:push-remote`. Nothing
# loads it implicitly. Prod Worker secrets are in no file at all — they are set
# with `wrangler secret put`.
